{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/news/further-appointment-of-tim-de-meyer-as-the-policing-member-of-the-sentencing-council","content_id":"4ff2e232-add9-48b8-befe-55dbd14dfb42","description":"The Lord Chancellor has approved the further appointment without competition of Tim De Meyer as policing member of the Sentencing Council from 1 July 2026 until the earlier of the date of the appointment of his successor or 30 June 2027. ","details":{"attachments":[],"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><p>The Lord Chancellor has approved the further appointment without competition of Tim De Meyer from 1 July 2026 until the earlier of the appointment of his successor or 30 June 2027.</p>\n\n<p>Ministers consulted the Commissioner for Public Appointments before making this appointment without competition. This is to ensure continuity of essential policing expertise on the Council while a full recruitment exercise is undertaken.</p>\n\n<h3 id=\"biography\">Biography</h3>\n\n<p>Tim De Meyer has 28 years of policing experience across a range of operational and strategic roles. He has served in the Metropolitan Police and Thames Valley Police. In 2023, he was appointed Chief Constable of Surrey Police. Since 2019, Tim has held the National Police Chiefs’ Council portfolio lead for Criminal Procedure and Investigations Act Disclosure, contributing to national policy and practice through the Criminal Justice Coordination Committee.</p>\n\n<p>He has declared no political activity.</p>\n\n<p>The Sentencing Council for England and Wales was established to promote greater transparency and consistency in sentencing, while maintaining the independence of the judiciary. The primary role of the council is to issue guidelines on sentencing, which the courts must follow unless it is in the interests of justice not to do so.</p>\n\n<p>The appointment of non-judicial members of the Sentencing Council, is regulated by the Commissioner for Public Appointments and recruitment processes comply with the Cabinet Office Governance Code on Public Appointments.</p>\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2026-05-28T08:00:00Z"}],"emphasised_organisations":["dcc907d6-433c-42df-9ffb-d9c68be5dc4d"],"images":[{"caption":null,"content_type":"image/jpeg","sources":{"s216":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a37db21ed915d5a62fdc763/s216_ministry-of-justice.jpg","s300":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a37db21e5274a7908e352d9/s300_ministry-of-justice.jpg","s465":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a37db2140f0b649cceb18ac/s465_ministry-of-justice.jpg","s630":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a37db21e5274a79051c925d/s630_ministry-of-justice.jpg","s712":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a37db2140f0b649cfaf7c16/s712_ministry-of-justice.jpg","s960":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a37db21ed915d5a62fdc762/s960_ministry-of-justice.jpg"},"type":"lead"}],"political":true},"document_type":"news_story","first_published_at":"2026-05-28T09:00:00+01:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/news/further-appointment-of-tim-de-meyer-as-the-policing-member-of-the-sentencing-council","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/news/further-appointment-of-tim-de-meyer-as-the-policing-member-of-the-sentencing-council","base_path":"/government/news/further-appointment-of-tim-de-meyer-as-the-policing-member-of-the-sentencing-council","content_id":"4ff2e232-add9-48b8-befe-55dbd14dfb42","document_type":"news_story","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-05-28T08:00:00Z","schema_name":"news_article","title":"Further appointment of Tim De Meyer as the policing member of the Sentencing Council","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/news/further-appointment-of-tim-de-meyer-as-the-policing-member-of-the-sentencing-council","withdrawn":false}],"emphasised_organisations":[{"analytics_identifier":"D18","api_path":"/